# Namespace, constants, and the data-driven expansion/season registry (loads first).
Constants.lua

# Centralised, defensive Blizzard-API wrappers + Secret-value safety (all risky calls live here).
Compat.lua

# Account-wide SavedVariables: schema, defaults, and the versioned migration framework.
Database.lua

# Combat-stat providers (Blizzard C_DamageMeter -> metadata-only), behind one interface.
Providers.lua

# The Mythic+ run lifecycle state machine: run / encounter / party tracking, reload recovery, dedupe.
Tracker.lua

# Derived data: party-member history aggregation, per-role stats, and personal bests.
History.lua

# Player scoring engine (fair, explainable, spec-aware). Config -> capability profiles -> normalize
# -> composition -> baselines -> category scorers -> weight redistribution -> overall + explanation.
Scoring\Config.lua
Scoring\Seasons\MidnightS1.lua
Scoring\Capability.lua
Scoring\Normalize.lua
Scoring\Composition.lua
Scoring\Distribute.lua
Scoring\Baselines.lua
Scoring\Healing.lua
Scoring\Categories.lua
Scoring\Weights.lua
Scoring\Score.lua
# Deterministic coaching review: category states -> "did well / work on" + recommendations.
Scoring\Review.lua
Scoring\Store.lua
Scoring\Tests.lua

# Returning-player recap service (local-only, anti-spam, role-aware).
Recap.lua

# Blizzard tooltip augmentation: your shared run history with a player, on unit + LFG tooltips.
Tooltip.lua

# Versioned, non-executable export / import.
Export.lua

# API self-check / diagnostics (validate the live API surface without running a key).
Diag.lua

# Live talent-inspection diagnostic for dispel capability (Debug page + /mldev inspect; not yet wired
# into scoring - validating reliability first).
Inspect.lua

# In-game "What's New" changelog.
Changelog.lua

# Central hero-tile config: icons + WoW-quality color scales for the Overview summary tiles.
HeroStats.lua

# All UI pages (one module page + internal tabs) and the post-run summary modal.
UI.lua

# Read-only "dungeon journal": per-season interrupt/dispel priorities, its own left-menu entry.
DungeonGuide.lua

# Read-only "how scoring works" reference (plain-language explainer of the live scoring model), own entry.
ScoringGuide.lua

# On-screen post-pull death report (overlay + party-chat post).
DeathReport.lua

# Module registration, lifecycle wiring, and slash commands (loads last).
Module.lua
